4. Printer Shares:
    
    -Oops! Someone accidentally sent an important file to a network printer can you retrieve it from the print server?
    
    -knowing how SMB protocol works would be helpful, smbclient and smbutil are good tools
    
    - SMB protocol:
        - Server Message Block - the language used to talk to each other to read/open/write/delete files remotely and access shared printers
        - port 445 SMB server(Samba on Linux) the path looks like \\server\sharename
        - Server = The machine the owns the folder/printer.  Role was played by Samba software,  Client = the machine that connects and browses/uses that share. tools like smbclient
        - What are the smbclient methods in SMB protocol?
        - Connection Syntax:
            - smbclient -L //<target> -N
                - -N = no password,  -L = List available shares <target> = IP address
            - smbclient -L //<target> -U <user>%<password> -p <portnumber>
                - <password> specifies password of user
            - smbclient //<target>/<share> -U <username> -c "commands”
                - -c used to specific commands in “” to execute non interactively
            - smbclient //<target>/<share> -U <username>%<password> -m <SMB2/3 or NT1>
                - <share> = folder name for accessing
                - -m maximum protocol that the client is willing to negotiate
                - starts an interactive session with smb:\> command prompt.
        - In-Session Commands:
            - Navigation - ls, cd <dir>, lcd <dir>, pwd
                - where lcd = change local directory(where downloads go)
            - Downloading files - get <filename>, mget <pattern>
                - get for single file and mget for multiple files
            - Uploading files - put <filename>, mput <pattern>
                - put for single file and mput for multiple files
            - recurse ON                  
            prompt OFF                     
            mget *
                - recurse = look all subdirectories, prompt = doesnot prompt for confirmation, * means select all
            - File/Directory Management - mkdir <dirname>, rmdir <dirname>, del <filename>, rename <old> <new>
            - Info/Permissions - dir, allinfo <filename>
                - dir displays all files and folders in current directory
                - allinfo displays file’s detailed metadata
            - Printer-related - print <filename>, queue
                - print is used to send file to shared printer
                - queue is used to view print queue
            - Exiting - exit, quit and Ctrl + D
