    - Ping:
        - used to check connectivity with a device using ICMP Echo Request and ICMP Echo Reply, measures RTT.
        - ping [options] <destination>
        - [options]
            - -c <number> (sends number of packets)
            - -i <time> (interval in seconds between packets)
            - -s <size> (sets packets size in bytes)
            - -t <time> (set TTL in number of hopes)
            - -f (flood ping, needs root)
            - -W <time> (sets time limit for the ping in seconds)
            - -4/-6 (force IPv4/IPv6)
            - -q (only summaries stats)
    - To use multiple commands in a single line
        - Unconditional Execution( ; )
            - command1 ; command 2 ; command 3
            - executes all commands
        - Conditional Success Execution(&&)
            - command1 && command2
            - it executes command2 when command1 succeed
        - Conditional Failure Execution( || )
            - command1 || command2
            - it executes command2 if command1 fails
        - Passing Output to Another Command( | )
            - command1 | command2
            - passes output of command1 to command2
        - Running a Command Inside Another( $(…) )
            - command1 $(command2) or command1 -$(command2)
            - first line uses the command2 output as argument for command1
            - second line uses the command2 output as option for command1
